Subject: [PATCH 2/5] C13, patch 2 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M19; main's
 fourth folder, item 3): THE LEDGER OF WALLS IS A GENERATED PAGE AMONG THE
 VIEWS, WITH ITS LOCK AND ITS ROW IN THE REGISTER

Main asks for a ledger of walls: a generated page among the views, one row a wall for the eight classes of
B1905's rows; for each, where it was first met, the arcs that prove a route impossible, the attempts by kind
of principle and how each ended, and the arcs whose question was found to be wrong.

WHAT IS BUILT. docs/views/LEDGER_OF_WALLS.md, written by the generator of the views (scripts/views/
generate.py) from B1905's rows and from nothing else. The generator reads B1905's script for its lists and
its reading of a row, compiled without an import. A table of eight rows, then a section a wall: where it
was first met; the arcs that settled their question without a pick; those whose question was found to be
wrong; those later corrected; and a table of what was tried, by kind of principle, with how it ended. The
gate that holds the views to their generators holds the page: seven views now.

THE PAGE PRINTS ARCS AND COUNTS, and no quotation and no outcome's text.

TWO READINGS ARE THE BUILDER'S, said on the page and asked of main on the card:
  - "first met" is the arc of the wall with the lowest number. Arcs are numbered in the order they were
    opened, and 184 of the 636 rows give no date.
  - "settled without a pick" stands for main's "prove a route impossible". The rows have no such column. It
    is: the row says the arc settled the question it asked, and its outcome has a word of main's list of
    denials and none of main's list of picks. A list of words, and the page says that it is no judgement.

THE LOCK, tests/test_ledger_of_walls.py, six tests. The page is what the generator makes of the rows. Its
counts are those of B1905's own tables, wall by wall and, for the four walls that script tabulates, kind by
kind. "First met" and "settled without a pick" are what the page says they are. No field of a row longer
than 24 characters stands on the page. Planted: a row added moves where a wall was first met; a class
changed moves two walls' counts; an outcome reworded to a pick takes its arc out of the list; and a twin,
the rows in another order, makes the same page. The generator leaves nothing beside B1905's script.

THE REGISTER: row P-837, for the ledger and the three things open about it (the classes have one reader
each; the two readings above; arcs that name neither subject in their verdict line or title were not read).
The count of rows that the register's checker holds is moved to 837.

Every gate passes but the count of landings. The lock, the locks of B1905, B1873 and B1858, and the 15 test
files that read the views or the register: 108 passed, 1 skipped. Not checked by main. Tested against
planted errors by the session that wrote it.
